  m_Name: texel-density
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: texel-density
    Term: Texel Density
    Abbreviation: 
    Category: 3
    Difficulty: 1
    ShortDefinition: How many texture pixels cover a given amount of world-space
      surface.
    SimpleExplanation: How sharp or muddy a texture looks for its real-world size.
    WhyItMatters: Consistent texel density keeps environments readable and fair across
      assets.
    Example: A door and nearby wall share roughly the same pixels-per-meter.
    CommonMistake: UV-scaling hero props denser than architecture, making walls look
      blurry by comparison.
    PracticePrompt: Measure texel density on three props and normalize them to one
      target value.
    GameUses:
    - Environment packing
    - LOD planning
    - QA art reviews
    RelatedTermIds:
    - uv-mapping
    - mipmap
    - texture-compression
    Tags:
    - texturing
    - uv
    - quality
    Synonyms: []
